---
smd: 2
title: Heading attributes in spec v2
summary: "Pins how spec v2 reads the braces that end a heading: a list is attributes only when it has items and each is #id, .class or key=value; an empty {} or a bare {word} is heading text, which the heading's id is made from. v2-hints.smd pins the same headings read with spec v1."
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-17
---

## Object {}

An empty `{}` is text: the heading reads "Object {}" and its id is `object-`.

## Returns {ok}

A bare word is text: the heading reads "Returns {ok}" and its id is `returns-ok`.

## Flags {agent}

`agent` without a value is a bare word too, so this section is not hidden from agents.

## Mixed {#mixed-id ok}

One bare word makes the whole list text, the `#mixed-id` included.

## Spaced { ok }

Text keeps its spaces as written.

## Setup {#setup-guide}

An id, a class and `key=value` items are attributes, as in spec v1: this heading reads "Setup" with the id `setup-guide`.

## Wide {.wide}

## Internal notes {agent=skip}

Hidden from the agent view.

<!-- smd-disable-next-line attrs/syntax -->
## Malformed {title="never closed}

A list that doesn't parse is text in both versions, and still an `attrs/syntax` error.

